      housing: "Bengals are high-energy, athletic cats that need significantly more space and activity than typical domestic cats. They climb, leap, and run constantly, so catios, leash walking and large multi-level cat furniture all earn their keep. The CFA confirms the water fascination that owners talk about, noting they may enjoy watching you brush your teeth or try to join you in the shower, and that they are quite trainable and often learn tricks. The door-opening and faucet-turning stories are widespread but unsourced, so treat them as folklore worth Bengal-proofing against rather than as documented breed behavior.",
