      enrichment: "Bengals are among the most active cat breeds studied, ranked alongside the Cornish Rex and Korat in a survey of 5,726 cats across 40 breeds. Budget 30 to 60 minutes of vigorous interactive play daily, plus access to safe outdoor exploration through a catio or leash, though that duration is a practical recommendation rather than a researched figure. Without adequate stimulation they become destructive and loud. They are highly trainable and enjoy leash walking, fetch and puzzle feeding. One common piece of advice worth pushing back on: a second active cat is not an automatic fix. The same study that ranked Bengals among the most active also ranked them high in aggression, and behavior traits in it were substantially heritable at 0.40 to 0.53, so a Bengal's intensity is temperament rather than boredom you can outsource to another cat. Judge the individual before adding a second.",
